    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "15. Stratagems",
    "ruleNumber": "15.09",
    "summary": "Snap Shooting needs permission from another rule. Pick one enemy unit no more than 24 inches from the firing unit, using that unit as the [visibility](vsdata:core-rule/visibility) observer. Follow [Making Attacks](vsdata:core-rule/making-attacks) and check each weapon's choice using the individual [attacking model's view](vsdata:core-rule/select-targets). Only a natural 6 hits, regardless of Ballistic Skill or modifiers. In the dated digital rule these hits have no Critical Hit status, and Hit rolls cannot be rerolled. The unit must wait for the next phase before starting an Action.",
